      "kind": "read_only_log_service_error",
      "detail": "First supplemental Cloud Build log read reported an internal error with adapter status 500. One read-only retry recovered the comparison and both startup receipts. The provider cause was not captured; the build itself succeeded once and was never resubmitted."
    },
    {
      "kind": "health_log_read_interruption",
      "detail": "Two observer-log reads reported an internal error with adapter status 500 and stopped the rollout after eleven verified functions. A later read recovered and accepted a timely natural deletion completion before work resumed. A further read after the thirteenth verified function exposed the underlying HTTP 429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED / RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED for Logging read requests (60 per minute); the Firebase client had masked it as 500. The verifier was changed to a single combined log query, preserving revision/time/event filters and all assertions, and retried only after backoff. Earlier error causes were not captured and are not retroactively proven. No deployment was repeated."
    },
    {
      "kind": "evidence_selection_guard",
